# TEMPLATE — copied to `allowed_domains` on first setup, then owned by the app.
#
# The live file is NOT tracked in git: the app rewrites it whenever an
# administrator saves Admin → Developer runtime, so tracking it meant every
# install produced a dirty working tree and, worse, offered up whatever
# addresses that operator had allow-listed (an internal host, a LAN IP) as a
# commit. Edit the allow-list in the admin UI; edit this file only to change
# what a NEW install starts with.
#
# Allowlisted egress destinations for notebook kernels (squid dstdomain).
# A leading dot matches all subdomains.
#
# PyPI (runtime pip install)
.pypi.org
.pythonhosted.org
# DuckDB extension registry — needed by lakehouse ETL nodes, which load the
# ducklake/postgres/httpfs extensions at run time. Without it the run fails
# with "Failed to download extension (HTTP 403)": squid refused it, not DuckDB.
.duckdb.org
# Direct LLM endpoints (only needed if users call providers directly; model
# calls via agentswarms.chat() are brokered by the platform and don't use this).
.openrouter.ai
.openai.com
